{"title":"Adding two-digit numbers without regrouping","key_idea":"When adding two-digit numbers, add the ones place first, then add the tens place, keeping each column separate.","method":["Write the numbers one below the other, lining up the ones and tens columns carefully.","Add the ones digits together: 4 + 3 = 7.","Add the tens digits together: 2 + 1 = 3.","Write the answer: 37."],"worked_example":{"problem":"32 + 15 = ?","steps":["Line up the tens and ones: 32 on top, 15 below.","Add the ones: 2 + 5 = 7.","Add the tens: 3 + 1 = 4.","Write the answer: 47."],"answer":"47"},"key_terms":[{"term":"ones place","meaning":"the rightmost digit in a number"},{"term":"tens place","meaning":"the second digit from the right"}],"common_mistakes":["Adding the digits in the wrong order or mixing up which column is ones and which is tens.","Forgetting to line up the numbers before adding."],"remember":"Always line up ones with ones and tens with tens.","quick_check":[{"q":"What is 41 + 36?","a":"77"},{"q":"What is 22 + 17?","a":"39"}],"tell_your_child":"When you add two-digit numbers, pretend each number is made of tens and ones in separate boxes. Add the ones first, then add the tens, and you will get the right answer."}
